{"data": [{"author_id": "332617373", "created_at": "2026-10-28T12:55:32.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115427246080954437"], "id": "2115427246080954437", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 9, "impression_count": 25614, "like_count": 81, "quote_count": 3, "reply_count": 10, "retweet_count": 11}, "text": "John Healey, UK Chancellor of the Exchequer, is presenting the first budget of Prime Minister Andy Burnham’s government.\nKey takeaways so far:\n• Fiscal Trajectory: Reinforces Britain’s multi-year fiscal consolidation path, with declining deficits and borrowing.\n• Headroom:", "url": "https://x.com/elerianm/status/2115427246080954437"}, {"author_id": "39125788", "created_at": "2026-10-28T12:25:27.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115419671877062710"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 177, "id": "239639973", "start": 166, "username": "ResObscura"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/mSZTlfZW9U", "end": 301, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/emollick/status/2115419671877062710/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2115419574166233088", "start": 278, "url": "https://t.co/mSZTlfZW9U"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/mSZTlfZW9U", "end": 301, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/emollick/status/2115419671877062710/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2115419574237577216", "start": 278, "url": "https://t.co/mSZTlfZW9U"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/mSZTlfZW9U", "end": 301, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/emollick/status/2115419671877062710/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2115419573985898496", "start": 278, "url": "https://t.co/mSZTlfZW9U"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/mSZTlfZW9U", "end": 301, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/emollick/status/2115419671877062710/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2115419574149509120", "start": 278, "url": "https://t.co/mSZTlfZW9U"}, {"display_url": "x.com/resobscura/sta…", "end": 325, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/resobscura/status/2115176788993380661", "start": 302, "url": "https://t.co/sQdnGxReAr"}]}, "id": "2115419671877062710", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 101, "impression_count": 22050, "like_count": 333, "quote_count": 2, "reply_count": 142, "retweet_count": 28}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2115176788993380661", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "There has been a bunch of really interesting experiments with activating individual neurons in open AI models, locking them into particular personas.\n\nHere historian @ResObscura tries the same trick with a model trained only on data before 1930, and the results are delightful. https://t.co/mSZTlfZW9U https://t.co/sQdnGxReAr", "url": "https://x.com/emollick/status/2115419671877062710"}, {"author_id": "279036722", "created_at": "2026-10-28T11:30:44.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115405905659355475"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/sb72FHMsFN", "end": 162, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/jasonfurman/status/2115405905659355475/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2115405775010963456", "start": 139, "url": "https://t.co/sb72FHMsFN"}]}, "id": "2115405905659355475", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 6, "impression_count": 8269, "like_count": 56, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 17, "retweet_count": 6}, "text": "In case you haven't paid attention to Treasury markets since the FOMC last met six weeks ago, here is an update: you didn't miss anything. https://t.co/sb72FHMsFN", "url": "https://x.com/jasonfurman/status/2115405905659355475"}, {"author_id": "332617373", "created_at": "2026-10-28T10:46:21.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115394735862898829"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/7h2pvtiNW0", "end": 301, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/elerianm/status/2115394735862898829/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2115394732117377024", "start": 278, "url": "https://t.co/7h2pvtiNW0"}]}, "id": "2115394735862898829", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 78, "impression_count": 41881, "like_count": 361, "quote_count": 10, "reply_count": 56, "retweet_count": 78}, "text": "Good morning.\nThe attached, from the Bloomberg article \"US-Friendly Nations Slash Treasury Purchases by 60%, Led by Asia,\" points to a development that I've been writing about: \nHistorically dependable buyers and holders of US government bonds have been pulling back, driven by https://t.co/7h2pvtiNW0", "url": "https://x.com/elerianm/status/2115394735862898829"}, {"author_id": "1214528593", "created_at": "2026-10-28T06:06:20.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115324264383651963"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/sandypuns_/sta…", "end": 100, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/sandypuns_/status/2115280509794414710", "start": 77, "url": "https://t.co/mYVVmFeMV7"}]}, "id": "2115324264383651963", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 4, "impression_count": 3564, "like_count": 51, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 3, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2115280509794414710", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "I don’t endorse the implication here at all but I do love a cheeky backronym https://t.co/mYVVmFeMV7", "url": "https://x.com/Miles_Brundage/status/2115324264383651963"}, {"author_id": "1214528593", "created_at": "2026-10-28T05:52:34.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115320799506944510"], "id": "2115320799506944510", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 3, "impression_count": 2135, "like_count": 27, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 14, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Something I think about from time to time is that even though language model tokens have gotten way cheaper, they were pretty cheap relative to “human tokens” from day one\n\nThis is a big part of why adoption took off so quickly compared to other technologies - it was born cheap", "url": "https://x.com/Miles_Brundage/status/2115320799506944510"}, {"author_id": "1214528593", "created_at": "2026-10-28T04:37:55.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115302016461488553"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/wtgowers/statu…", "end": 139, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/wtgowers/status/2115008335154176006", "start": 116, "url": "https://t.co/Zxvao29kGG"}]}, "id": "2115302016461488553", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 3111, "like_count": 16, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 3, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2115008335154176006", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Mathematicians question the “shepherding” approach (giving the results to a small group of physicists to deal with) https://t.co/Zxvao29kGG", "url": "https://x.com/Miles_Brundage/status/2115302016461488553"}, {"author_id": "279036722", "created_at": "2026-10-28T03:45:40.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115288866454442281"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/hgIYfcvYzJ", "end": 289, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/jasonfurman/status/2115288866454442281/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2115288325258911744", "start": 266, "url": "https://t.co/hgIYfcvYzJ"}]}, "id": "2115288866454442281", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 85, "impression_count": 39538, "like_count": 242, "quote_count": 8, "reply_count": 21, "retweet_count": 6}, "text": "Three of my five Claude accounts maxed out working on all the ideas I've gotten for improving Econvitals!\n\n(If I was more efficient about model selection and token usage I wouldn't be in this situation, so this is as much evidence of incompetence as anything else.) https://t.co/hgIYfcvYzJ", "url": "https://x.com/jasonfurman/status/2115288866454442281"}, {"author_id": "1214528593", "created_at": "2026-10-28T03:19:40.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115282321830298010"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/willdepue/stat…", "end": 169, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/willdepue/status/2115264175421431894", "start": 146, "url": "https://t.co/9P2jmhcKxt"}]}, "id": "2115282321830298010", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 10, "impression_count": 6056, "like_count": 51, "quote_count": 3, "reply_count": 5, "retweet_count": 1}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2115264175421431894", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Still don’t think most people are aware of the fact that Hacktron could have taken images from *any* Slacks, not just OpenAI’s, a few months back https://t.co/9P2jmhcKxt", "url": "https://x.com/Miles_Brundage/status/2115282321830298010"}, {"author_id": "39125788", "created_at": "2026-10-28T02:59:39.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115277286123704654"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/ArtificialAnly…", "end": 301, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/ArtificialAnlys/status/2115265171233120627", "start": 278, "url": "https://t.co/YKPok303dd"}]}, "id": "2115277286123704654", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 278, "impression_count": 110015, "like_count": 1470, "quote_count": 27, "reply_count": 215, "retweet_count": 96}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2115265171233120627", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Artificial Analysis finally moves to closed benchmarks (goodbye GDPval-AA), and finds that open weights models are falling  further behind than they had previously measured. Take with a grain of salt, but matches the general vibes that we haven't seen a Fable-class open model. https://t.co/YKPok303dd", "url": "https://x.com/emollick/status/2115277286123704654"}, {"author_id": "39125788", "created_at": "2026-10-28T02:43:30.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115273222061015169"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/jkZf7HKVQu", "end": 308, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/emollick/status/2115273222061015169/video/1", "media_key": "13_2115272646942167040", "start": 285, "url": "https://t.co/jkZf7HKVQu"}]}, "id": "2115273222061015169", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 98, "impression_count": 32598, "like_count": 527, "quote_count": 16, "reply_count": 82, "retweet_count": 32}, "text": "Genie 4: \"Scene: A Victorian high tea. Character: A mouse in appropriate garb.\"\n\"A porcupine walks by\"\n\"The mouse grows wings\"\n\"The mouse flies to the teacup\"\nThis is realtime &amp; I can walk around freely.\n\nIt is glitchy, but also impossibly advanced compared to a couple years ago. https://t.co/jkZf7HKVQu", "url": "https://x.com/emollick/status/2115273222061015169"}, {"author_id": "279036722", "created_at": "2026-10-28T02:08:20.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115264372079808752"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/jennjwang/stat…", "end": 290, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/jennjwang/status/2115119079652466814", "start": 267, "url": "https://t.co/wodzUyQrif"}]}, "id": "2115264372079808752", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 47, "impression_count": 13969, "like_count": 85, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 4, "retweet_count": 11}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2115119079652466814", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "O*NET tracks the tasks that are required by different jobs. It has been invaluable for research. But it also was clear that it could be improved a lot--and the need to improve it was much greater than ever. So very glad to see this, looks like we'll all be using it. https://t.co/wodzUyQrif", "url": "https://x.com/jasonfurman/status/2115264372079808752"}, {"author_id": "1214528593", "created_at": "2026-10-28T00:44:18.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115243223388147779"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/willdepue/stat…", "end": 300, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/willdepue/status/2115236836092313988", "start": 277, "url": "https://t.co/7cCL0zr09S"}]}, "id": "2115243223388147779", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 4, "impression_count": 2654, "like_count": 32, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 9, "retweet_count": 1}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2115236836092313988", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "There are legislators who are really on top of export controls, and others who are really on top of frontier AI safety, but no one has really set out to make this their top issue (AI security in the original sense, not safety rebranded as security).\n\nI hope that changes soon! https://t.co/7cCL0zr09S", "url": "https://x.com/Miles_Brundage/status/2115243223388147779"}, {"author_id": "612896910", "created_at": "2026-10-27T23:10:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115219491122479544"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 101, "start": 93, "tag": "BLSdata"}], "urls": [{"description": "The .gov means it's official. Federal government websites often end in .gov or .mil. Before sharing sensitive information, make sure you're on a federal government site. The site is secure. The https:// ensures that you are connecting to the official website and that any information you provide is encrypted and transmitted securely. Median weekly earnings of the nation’s 110.9 million full-time wage and salary workers age 25 and over were $1,307 in the third quarter of 2026. This was 2.0 percent higher", "display_url": "bls.gov/opub/ted/2026/…", "end": 92, "expanded_url": "https://www.bls.gov/opub/ted/2026/median-weekly-earnings-by-educational-attainment-third-quarter-2026.htm", "images": [{"height": 126, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2115111026496552960/41T1NGUV?format=png&name=orig", "width": 228}, {"height": 126, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2115111026496552960/41T1NGUV?format=png&name=150x150", "width": 126}], "start": 69, "status": 200, "title": "Median weekly earnings by educational attainment, third quarter 2026 : The Economics Daily : U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics", "unwound_url": "https://www.bls.gov/opub/ted/2026/median-weekly-earnings-by-educational-attainment-third-quarter-2026.htm", "url": "https://t.co/Tzb1yG3ryo"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/G7g0ZZbktV", "end": 125, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/BLS_gov/status/2115219491122479544/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2115179201242300416", "start": 102, "url": "https://t.co/G7g0ZZbktV"}]}, "id": "2115219491122479544", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 2785, "like_count": 6, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Median weekly earnings by educational attainment, third quarter 2026 https://t.co/Tzb1yG3ryo #BLSdata https://t.co/G7g0ZZbktV", "url": "https://x.com/BLS_gov/status/2115219491122479544"}, {"author_id": "279036722", "created_at": "2026-10-27T23:05:21.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115218322820370551"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 51, "id": "10778572", "start": 44, "username": "delong"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/delong/status/…", "end": 202, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/delong/status/2115167271962501340", "start": 179, "url": "https://t.co/gqqPjJ2nP7"}]}, "id": "2115218322820370551", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 15, "impression_count": 11160, "like_count": 50, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2115167271962501340", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "I really appreciate your thoughtful writeup @delong, both on the site itself and my thoughts on the where the Fed should be now.\n\nWe're entering a wild, scary and exciting world. https://t.co/gqqPjJ2nP7", "url": "https://x.com/jasonfurman/status/2115218322820370551"}, {"author_id": "39125788", "created_at": "2026-10-27T22:31:26.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115209786157412397"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/djlVFyPcQo", "end": 301, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/emollick/status/2115209786157412397/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2115209770760126465", "start": 278, "url": "https://t.co/djlVFyPcQo"}, {"display_url": "x.com/AlexTamkin/sta…", "end": 325, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/AlexTamkin/status/2115190544905433315", "start": 302, "url": "https://t.co/acaYdzoCTm"}]}, "id": "2115209786157412397", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 238, "impression_count": 41619, "like_count": 568, "quote_count": 50, "reply_count": 294, "retweet_count": 75}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2115190544905433315", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Important, but not unexpected, finding that experts working with AI agents are swayed by the positions of the AI, even if they think they are working independently.\n\nIf your independent judgement matters on a task, you need to be deliberate about when in the process to use AI. https://t.co/djlVFyPcQo https://t.co/acaYdzoCTm", "url": "https://x.com/emollick/status/2115209786157412397"}, {"author_id": "1214528593", "created_at": "2026-10-27T21:32:23.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115194926065701308"], "id": "2115194926065701308", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 4223, "like_count": 122, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 7, "retweet_count": 5}, "text": "I’m a centrist in that I thought Obama’s Cheesecake Factory joke was funny and also I like Cheesecake Factory", "url": "https://x.com/Miles_Brundage/status/2115194926065701308"}, {"author_id": "1214528593", "created_at": "2026-10-27T20:28:35.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115178872035811828"], "id": "2115178872035811828", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 3, "impression_count": 2766, "like_count": 13, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Bet some folks are working overtime to add texting functionality to Muse / dots / Duet \n\n(Otherwise I dunno what they’re thinking! Would immediately differentiate, at least for a few days. I don’t want another app/sub-app)", "url": "https://x.com/Miles_Brundage/status/2115178872035811828"}, {"author_id": "39125788", "created_at": "2026-10-27T18:36:22.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115150629836632473"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/codytfenwick/s…", "end": 306, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/codytfenwick/status/2114941993897828365", "start": 283, "url": "https://t.co/aCAdm2iu9q"}]}, "id": "2115150629836632473", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 27, "impression_count": 24530, "like_count": 238, "quote_count": 4, "reply_count": 75, "retweet_count": 6}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2114941993897828365", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "The repeated argument that AI companies are talking about existential risks as a way of creating hype &amp; inflating their stock prices has always been odd.\n\nTelling people your product may murder everyone does not, in fact, encourage people to adopt it or reduce regulatory risks. https://t.co/aCAdm2iu9q", "url": "https://x.com/emollick/status/2115150629836632473"}, {"author_id": "39125788", "created_at": "2026-10-27T17:04:34.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115127527241085010"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/akilUHGgYn", "end": 265, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/emollick/status/2115127527241085010/video/1", "media_key": "13_2115127325356429312", "start": 242, "url": "https://t.co/akilUHGgYn"}]}, "id": "2115127527241085010", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 137, "impression_count": 65307, "like_count": 618, "quote_count": 12, "reply_count": 64, "retweet_count": 37}, "text": "Genie 4 runs DOOM: \"Walking through a typical office but every computer is running DOOM and all of the walls are also running DOOM and also everything is DOOM\"\n\n\"My coworker who is a demon appears\"\n\n\"He has a chaingun\"\n\n\"He gives me a bonus\" https://t.co/akilUHGgYn", "url": "https://x.com/emollick/status/2115127527241085010"}, {"author_id": "825088493764407298", "created_at": "2026-10-27T16:56:14.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115123481767809499", "2115125429619343609"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 18, "id": "15460048", "start": 14, "username": "MIT"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/sequoia/status…", "end": 296, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/sequoia/status/2115111389501218868", "start": 273, "url": "https://t.co/cChFwfLpgU"}]}, "id": "2115125429619343609", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 550, "impression_count": 106175, "like_count": 1361, "quote_count": 9, "reply_count": 62, "retweet_count": 50}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2115111389501218868", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Every winter, @MIT has run a 1-month class (6.9630) in which students make poker AIs and compete against each other for cash prizes. Coding agents have accelerated that process so much that it's now possible to build a poker bot in an *hour*.\n\nAlso, I'll be at the finals! https://t.co/cChFwfLpgU", "url": "https://x.com/polynoamial/status/2115125429619343609"}, {"author_id": "825088493764407298", "created_at": "2026-10-27T16:48:29.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115123481767809499", "2115125429619343609"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 18, "id": "15460048", "start": 14, "username": "MIT"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/sequoia/status…", "end": 266, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/sequoia/status/2115111389501218868", "start": 243, "url": "https://t.co/cChFwfLpgU"}]}, "id": "2115123481767809499", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 13, "impression_count": 3877, "like_count": 38, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 3, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2115111389501218868", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Every winter, @MIT has run a 1-month class (6.9630) in which students make poker AIs and compete against each other for cash prizes. Coding agents have accelerated that process so much that it's now possible to build a poker bot in an *hour*. https://t.co/cChFwfLpgU", "url": "https://x.com/polynoamial/status/2115123481767809499"}, {"author_id": "279036722", "created_at": "2026-10-27T16:41:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115121596079956176"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/xHjB7WePGX", "end": 296, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/jasonfurman/status/2115121596079956176/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2115075723027238912", "start": 273, "url": "https://t.co/xHjB7WePGX"}]}, "id": "2115121596079956176", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 19, "impression_count": 11199, "like_count": 86, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 15, "retweet_count": 10}, "text": "When the Fed doesn't move tomorrow the US will still have among the highest real policy rates of any of the major central banks in the world--a turnaround from the past when we tended to be on the low end.\n\nDue to a combo of our strong growth &amp; inflationary pressures. https://t.co/xHjB7WePGX", "url": "https://x.com/jasonfurman/status/2115121596079956176"}, {"autho